inyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:41:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:47:    Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:48:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:146:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid LR-symmetric 3x3 masks, keyed by active pixel count.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:169:    \"\"\"Generate a random LR-symmetric 3x3 pattern using two colors (guaranteed non-uniform).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:181:    \"\"\"Pick a random valid minority mask (uniform over active count, then uniform within count).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:187:    \"\"\"Find all (t, l) offsets where the given subset of active cells is consistent with mask.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:206:    \"\"\"Choose a subset of active mask positions that uniquely determines the placement.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:222:    \"\"\"Pixel origin of cell (i, j) interior within the full grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:227:    \"\"\"Construct a 29x29 grid: fill all cells with majority, then overwrite active_cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:238:    \"\"\"Single generation attempt: build output, choose input subset, verify with solver.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b99e7126.py:264:def generate_input():\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:15:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:16:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:19:    Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:24:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:29:    Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:31:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/996ec1f3.py:198:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:5:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:6:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:9:    Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:13:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:18:    Key insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:19:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/981571dc.py:100:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py:61:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py:62:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py:81:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py:290:    \"\"\"Reserve enough evidence for the solver to infer every block and separator.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py:360:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:31:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:32:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:51:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:142:    \"\"\"Sample source rectangle dimensions under the output-width budget.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:202:    \"\"\"Generate one valid input grid, or None when sampled dimensions fail constraints.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py:226:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:35:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:36:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:39:    Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:45:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:51:    Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:52:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:422:    \"\"\"Build waypoint list for a random polyline with axis ax (0=vert-primary, 1=horiz-primary).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:456:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:891:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:5:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:6:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:9:    Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:13:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:18:    Key insight: Tile dimensions are unknown and must be inferred; prefer the smallest tile with genuine repetition over one that memorizes the entire region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:19:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/135a2760.py:121:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
